# Admin Dashboard Rules

Before generating any admin UI, always read:

- docs/PROJECT_RULES.md
- docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
- docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md

Never violate these documents.

---

# Objective

Build a premium, minimal, modern CMS.

The dashboard should feel like professional software instead of a template.

Design inspiration:

- Vercel Dashboard
- Stripe Dashboard
- Shopify Admin
- Linear
- Notion

Avoid copying layouts.

Follow their design principles.

---

# Dashboard Philosophy

The dashboard should feel:

- Professional
- Clean
- Fast
- Spacious
- Modern
- Calm

Avoid:

- Bright colours
- Gradient overload
- Heavy shadows
- Glassmorphism
- Bootstrap admin templates
- Overly colourful interfaces

The interface should never compete with the content.

---

# Layout

Every admin page should follow:

Sidebar

↓

Top Header

↓

Page Header

↓

Content

↓

Footer

Maintain the same spacing across all pages.

---

# Sidebar

Dark background.

Collapsible.

Logo at top.

Grouped navigation.

Lucide icons only.

Current page highlighted.

Keep sidebar width consistent.

Never create multiple sidebar styles.

---

# Header

Sticky.

Contains:

Search

Notifications

Profile

Breadcrumb

Quick Actions (optional)

Never overload the header.

---

# Page Header

Every page must include:

Title

↓

Short Description

↓

Primary Action Button (optional)

↓

Divider

---

# Cards

Use one consistent card design.

White background.

Rounded corners.

Soft border.

Subtle shadow.

Comfortable padding.

Never create multiple card styles.

---

# Tables

Use TanStack Table.

Include:

Search

Pagination

Sorting

Empty State

Loading State

Responsive layout

Avoid heavy borders.

No dark table headers.

---

# Forms

Only use shadcn/ui.

Each form should include:

Label

Placeholder

Validation

Error Message

Helper Text

Loading State

Disabled State

Required Indicator (when applicable)

Never build custom form controls unless necessary.

---

# Buttons

Allowed variants:

Primary

Secondary

Outline

Ghost

Destructive

Use shadcn/ui Button.

Do not create custom button components.

---

# Dialogs

Use AlertDialog or Dialog from shadcn/ui.

Use dialogs for:

Delete

Confirmation

Image Preview

Settings

Large Forms

Dialogs should:

Be centered.

Have clear titles.

Provide Cancel and Confirm actions.

Support Escape to close.

---

# Toasts

Use React-hot toast.

Success

Error

Warning

Info

Keep messages concise.

Never block the UI.

---

# Navigation

Use Breadcrumbs.

Highlight active navigation.

Maintain consistent spacing.

Avoid deeply nested menus.

Maximum nesting:

Two levels.

---

# Empty States

Every module should include an Empty State.

Display:

Icon

Title

Short description

Primary Action

Example:

No gallery images found.

[Upload Image]

Never leave blank screens.

---

# Loading States

Use Skeleton components.

Maintain page layout while loading.

Avoid full-page spinners.

---

# Error States

Friendly language.

Retry button.

Never expose technical details.

---

# Search

Position above tables.

Responsive.

Debounce if needed.

Provide clear "No results" state.

---

# Filters

Compact layout.

Wrap on smaller screens.

Always provide:

Reset Filters

Clear Filters

---

# Pagination

Bottom aligned.

Simple controls.

Highlight current page.

Keep layout consistent.

---

# Image Upload

Use drag and drop.

Show preview.

Display upload progress.

Allow remove before saving.

Validate:

File type

File size

Show errors immediately.

---

# Icons

Lucide React only.

Sizes:

20px

24px

32px

Never mix icon libraries.

---

# Animations

Use Framer Motion.

Allowed:

Fade

Slide

Scale

Hover

Avoid:

Bounce

Flip

Rotate

Elastic

Animation should feel natural.

---

# Responsive Design

Desktop

Full Sidebar

Tablet

Collapsible Sidebar

Mobile

Drawer Navigation

No horizontal scrolling.

---

# Accessibility

Keyboard navigation.

Visible focus states.

Semantic HTML.

Proper labels.

ARIA attributes where required.

---

# Component Reuse

Always reuse:

PageHeader

DashboardCard

DataTable

EmptyState

Loader

DeleteDialog

ConfirmDialog

SearchBar

FilterBar

ImageUploader

Never duplicate these components.

---

# Styling

Use TailwindCSS.

Use CSS variables.

Never hardcode colours.

Never hardcode spacing.

Follow DESIGN_SYSTEM.md.

---

# Never Do

Never redesign existing components without instruction.

Never create multiple button styles.

Never create multiple card styles.

Never introduce new colour palettes.

Never use Bootstrap.

Never use Material UI.

Never use random icon libraries.

Never hardcode UI text that should come from CMS.

---

# Final Rule

Every admin page should feel like it belongs to the same product.

Consistency is more important than creativity.

When in doubt:

Reuse existing components.